 "response": "Mifa's budget is now **$1825K**.\n\n**How the records were applied**\n- Only Finance Office budget lines count (set, increase, decrease). Messages from other teams and Finance notes that don't change the budget were ignored.\n- For each withdrawal chain, I worked backward from the last withdrawal, which has not itself been withdrawn. Each withdrawal cancels the one before it in the chain, so whether an update stands depends on how many active withdrawals sit above it. Examples:\n  - #0005 (+$543K) stands. #0040 withdrew it, but #0599 withdrew #0040.\n  - #0004 (\u2212$143K) is cancelled. #0012 withdrew it, #0136 withdrew #0012, and #1024 withdrew #0136, so #0012 is back in force.\n  - #0009 (+$464K) is cancelled. In the chain #0016 \u2190 #0063 \u2190 #0071 \u2190 #0076 \u2190 #0117 \u2190 #0454 \u2190 #0818, #0016 ends up in force.\n- About 130 budget updates are cancelled this way. All other updates were applied in order, starting from the $1040K set in #0001.\n\n**Running total (selected checkpoints)**\n\n| After record | Budget |\n|---|---|\n| #0005 (+$543K) | $1583K |\n| #0100 (\u2212$371K) | $2346K |\n| #0409 (+$95K) | $4004K |\n| #0540 (\u2212$524K) | $3891K |\n| #0926 (withdrawn later; total after #0919) | $2489K |\n| #1036 (\u2212$486K) | $2018K |\n| #1300 area (#1299, \u2212$135K) | $1990K |\n| #1599 (+$150K), the last change | $1825K |\n\nANSWER: $1825K",
